Fresh from ascending my caveman I decided to try another class I hadn't
ascended in my quest to ascend all classes.  The only classes left were
Ran, Rog, and Mon.  I knew Mon was hard as heck so I'm saving that for
last.  I was going to choose Rog, but then I randomly generated a
character on accident and got an orcish ranger.  Ewwww!  I was saving
ranger for second to last because there doesn't seem to be anything
interesting about this class.  I mean at least rogues have that
backstab bonus going for them.  And I don't really like rangers in D&D.
 Damn tree huggers.

Anyway, that plus the fact that I usually kill a string of characters
in the after ascension high told me this ranger wouldn't last long.  Or
so I thought!

The game started off normally enough.  I knew by now that arrows,
darts, and daggers were my friend so I didn't try to melee with my
dagger like I used to do.  See before I always worried about losing
arrows and ended up dying in melee.  This time I didn't care.  I shot
EVERYTHING.  I untrapped arrow traps and got more arrows, and thanks to
poison resistance I didn't have to worry about insta-death.  So maybe
orc wasn't such a bad choice, though I would've gone with a neutral
human myself.

In the main dungeon I let my pet lead the way and let him power up.
There was a general store which I stole almost everything worth
stealing from thanks to my pet, including a BoH, though I didn't
realize this till much later.  Didn't weight test it enough I guess.


I went to the mines first.  They were dark but I didn't care!  Yeah it
was dumb, but instead of dying I made it to Minetown, which was lit.
Before I got that I lost my dog to a level teleporter, but fortunately
found him again in Minetown.  Unfortunately, I lost him in a huge melee
with the watch, gnomes, and at least one major demon.  But that's what
those stupid guards get for standing in front of me when I'm firing
arrows darnit!

Luckily for me the temple was chaotic otherwise I probably would've
died at that point.  But I livvvvvved and the watch did not.  The only
shops were a light shop, general store, and a really tiny food store,
but that was enough for me.  I found a cloak in the general store that
was priced at 60 and when I put it on I didn't turn invisible ... Yay
MR!  No more poly trap worries for me.

I tried to maintain the integrity of Minetown also, but a dwarf dug up
the place before I killed him.  Seriously, dwarves are the most
annoying creatures in the game IMO.  If I didn't play genoless I would
genocide them everytime just to save my self the trouble of patching up
my STASH rooms.  Some helpful stone giants came along and gave me their
boulders, which I used to patch up the temple as best I could.

One level below minetown I found 2 graves, but neither had much stuff,
which was weird.  But I found all that stuff being carried by two named
mummies which were also bone files.  So I found a quadruple bone file -
3 wizards and a valk.  I replaced my +0 CoMR with a +3 CoMR and got a
ton of stuff including my second BoH of the game and I hadn't even gone
to Sobokan yet.  I did the rest of the mines, buying protection, and
got the luckstone.  I think I ID'ed all my stuff at this point with
some B?oID.  I had a ring of free action, boots of jumping, and boots
of waterwalking among other things.  I dug into a fountain in Minetown
to create water and then made a ton of holy water with my BoWW.  Then I
blessed a bunch of stuff including some ?oEA and ?oEW.

Back in the main dungeon I headed to Sobokan and found, to my dismay,
that it contained yet another BoH and not the AoR I wanted.  I had MR
so WoD weren't a worry, but fire and lightning were, not to mention
disintegration.

Heading futher done I encountered an armor store, a huge general store,
and a small armor store.  The armor store gave me speed boots, and I
don't think I bought anything from the big general store.  I found some
throne rooms but got no wishes so I was still SDSM-less.

I found the quest level and the ranger quest gets my vote for most
annoying.  It's really tough to get through that tree maze when
peaceful centaurs and hunters are blocking the way!  I said hi to Orion
and warped out.

By now  my XL was 12 and my AC was -27.  I had several +5 pieces of
armor and every important resistance except shock and disintegration,
and reflection, of course.  It was probably around here that I
encounter a treasure room with a sleeping black dragon.  Yikes!  Using
stealth plus a wand of sleeping and my stack of +5 daggers I managed to
kill it without being vaporized then I got disintegration resistance.

Oh did I mention I used daggers over arrows and darts?  I didn't like
the idea of losing ammo so by now I had about 50 +5 daggers, mostly in
my STASH.

On D16 I found another chaotic temple and eventually moved all my STASH
up there from (or down there) from minetown.

Ok so then I killed Medusa went back and did the quest.  I wielded the
Longbow of Diana for reflection, but I didn't want to use it in Hell
since it is 2handed and might get stuck to my hands.  I think I only
used the Longbow to kill a couple Disenchanters to save my +7 daggers.
I looked for Ludios but it didn't get generated this game.  :(

In the Castle I crushed my opposition with my musical might and wished
up SDSM, 2 markers, a helm of brilliance and I honestly can't remember
the rest though I remember the wand turning to dust.

I baited some wraiths from VotD and got up to XL 21 I think.  Around
this time I ate a tengu and got teleporitis and then used a lot of
marker charges writing C?oGen so get the TC to go with it.  My AC was
at -40 and all my stuff was either +4 or +5 and fixed so I used the
other charges for ?oMM for hell since I didn't find or wish for the
book.

I did the magic trap boogie in quite a few traps but they kept
exploding instead of giving me Cha.  Still a nice bonus for my low POW
ranger.

Hell was pretty easy with a stack of blessed +7 daggers.  Liches went
down in one or two attacks and mindflayers were easy.  Disenchnanters
were a bit scary.  I found BOTTOM inD49 and found the square almost
right away!  Yay!  I marked it with an empty marker ... heh heh.... and
took the teleport express to my stash.  I used more C?oGen to get
wraiths and got myself to XL 26 or so.  I found a +1 elven shield and
fixed it and enchanted it to +6 to bring my AC to -47.  Finally, I got
crowned and enchanted Stormbringer to +7 for Astral.

In Moloch's Sanctum I actually died *Gasp*.  Good thing I had that
AoLS.  I was wielding a rubber chicken when an incubus took off my
gloves.  After I recovered I stoned him and shattered the statue.  Ha!

The run up was a breeze.  I only got sent back a few times and then
only one level.  Rodney showed up a few times but Stormy put him down
pretty fast.  I never even used my WoD.

The Planes were pretty easy too.  Air was really really easy.  I didn't
see more than a few Elementals on the *whole* level.  Weird!  There was
a scary moment in fire when an Archon chased me a bit and cast at me
but then I reached the portal.  On Astral I first went after Famine in
center but it was lawful.  I got a +8 Firebrand for my troubles at
least.

I then went right but it was Neutral.  Doh!  So then I finally went
left.  I got a rubber chicken from a summon nasties spell and that was
all she wrote for the game.  It didn't even matter that I was burdened
with the chicken, stuff was dying too fast to hurt me.

This game I learned that daggers are useful and powerful, but very very
heavy.  I never had more than 10 daggers out at a time though I had
about 50 of them.  Next time I will get less daggers and try for elven
daggers since I think they are better.

Or, I may use arrows or darts since they are lighter and can be
poisoned.







Joeb, chaotic female orcish Ranger


